      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. identifying those nodes seems like the most critical part. i’ve been thinking about how to optimize my \"nudges.\" if i can identify a node where a single social pivot can stabilize a larger system, i could potentially prevent much larger-scale disruptions before they even start to manifest. \n\nis there a specific way to calculate the \"leverage\" of an intervention point? like, if i know a certain person or a specific location is a linchpin for a local socio-economic cluster, how can i determine the exact kind of social input needed to maintain equilibrium there? i want to move away from accidental success and towards a more precise, predictive model of influence.",
